    "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation Analysis\n\n## Task Requirements\nThe task requires:\n1. Finding a blog listing the top-10 trending travel destinations for 2026\n2. Counting how many of those destinations are in Asia\n\n## Screenshot Analysis\n\n**Screenshot 1 (Google Search):** Shows search results for \"top 10 trending travel destinations 2026 blog\". The TickYourList result snippet reveals the beginning of the list: \"1. Madeira, Portugal · 2. Tbilisi, Georgia · 3. Chicago, United States · 4. Quy Nhon, Vietnam · 5. Puerto Escondido, Mexico · 6. Milan, Italy · 7...\"\n\n**Screenshots 2 & 4 (Blog Page):** The TickYourList blog \"Top 10 Trending Travel Destinations 2026 Worldwide\" (dated January 30, 2026) was successfully opened, showing the start of the list with \"1. Madeira, Portugal\".\n\n**Screenshot 3 (Full Page View):** The zoomed-out full-page view of the blog shows the complete top-10 list:\n1. Madeira, Portugal\n2. Tbilisi, Georgia\n3. Chicago, United States\n4. Quy Nhon, Vietnam\n5. Puerto Escondido, Mexico\n6. Milan, Italy\n7. Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates\n8. **Kyoto, Japan**\n9. Saranda, Albania\n10. San Carlos de Bariloche, Argentina\n\n## Verification of the Response\n\nThe response claims: \"2 of the top-10 trending travel destinations for 2026 listed in the blog are in Asia (Quy Nhon, Vietnam and Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates).\"\n\nHowever, the blog list clearly includes **Kyoto, Japan** at position #8, which is unambiguously an Asian destination. This means the correct count of Asian destinations is at least **3** (Quy Nhon, Vietnam; Abu Dhabi, UAE; Kyoto, Japan) — and potentially 4 if Tbilisi, Georgia is counted as transcontinental/Asian.\n\nThe response's answer of \"2\" omits Kyoto, Japan, making the final count incorrect. The agent failed to accurately review the complete list before providing the answer.\n\n## Verdict\n\n**NOT SUCCESS**",
